course: dictionary
lesson: 7304
title: Words that show feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words tell you how someone feels without saying it straight out. «"Mayn't I sing them just one little song?" he pleaded piteously.» He is begging, and the words sound small and sad. So piteously must mean very sadly, in a way that makes people want to help.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Pleaded means begged, so piteously tells you how he begged. A check helps: put «very sadly» in the place of piteously and see if the sentence still makes sense. It does, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Writers use words like this to show a character's pain without spelling it out. «A puppy whines piteously» tells you the puppy is hurt or lonely, and you feel sorry for it too.
fact: Piteously is an adverb: it tells us how something is done, such as how someone pleads or how a puppy whines.
fact: «Piteously» means in a way that makes people feel pity, very sadly.
fact: «Pleaded» means begged for something, often in a very earnest way.
fact: In stories, «Alice cries in the pool of tears» and «Toad weeps in his dungeon» show characters in great distress.
fact: To check a meaning, swap in your idea and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «"Mayn't I sing them just one little song?" he pleaded piteously.» What does piteously mean here? | In a cheerful, bouncy way | *In a way that makes people feel pity, very sadly | Very quickly, so no one could hear | In a loud, angry shout
exercise: «A puppy whines piteously.» What does the author want the reader to feel? | Bored of the noise | *Sorry for the puppy | Excited about a walk | Annoyed with the puppy
exercise: «He pleaded piteously for one more song.» Find and copy one word that means begged. | more | song | one | *pleaded
test: «Toad weeps piteously in his dungeon.» What does piteously tell us about Toad? | He is hungry and wants his dinner | *He is very sad, and we feel sorry for him | He is singing a happy tune | He is far away from the dungeon
test: Which word is closest in meaning to piteously? | Quietly | Angrily | Cheerfully | *Sadly
exam: Which sentence shows someone speaking piteously? | "Let's race to the gate!" she shouted. | *"Please, please let me go," she sobbed, shaking. | "Good morning!" she said with a big smile. | "Pass the salt, please."
